ईर् cl. 2. Ā. ई॑र्ते (3. pl. ई॑रते, AV.; RV.), ईरं-चक्रे, ईरिष्यति, ऐरिष्ट, ईरितुम्;
 Ved. inf. इर॑ध्यै, RV. i, 134, 2, to go, move, rise, arise from, RV.;
to go away, retire, AV. xix, 38, 2;
to agitate, elevate, raise (one's voice), RV. :
Caus. P. ईर॑यति (cf. √ ईल्), to agitate, throw, cast;
to excite, RV.; AV.; MBh.; R. &c.;
to cause to rise;
to bring to life;
 to raise one's voice, utter, pronounce, proclaim, cite, RV.; ChUp.; Ragh.; Suśr. &c. ;
to elevate, RV.; VS.; TS.; ŚBr. : Ā. to raise one's self, AV.; VS.
